IMPORT daydate

§ `DateTime Definitions and Helpers`

-- DATETIME is an absolute point in time.
-- Uses document TIMEZONE by default; can override with explicit tz parameter (IANA string).
-- Stored internally as UTC; extractors return LOCAL values in the stored timezone.


§§ `DateTime Constructors`

-- Datetime date time  -> uses document TIMEZONE
GIVEN date IS A DATE
      t    IS A TIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %t% on %date% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ date t TIMEZONE

-- Datetime date time tz  -> explicit IANA timezone string
GIVEN date IS A DATE
      t    IS A TIME
      tz   IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %t% on %date% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ date t tz

-- Datetime date h m s  -> via Time h m s + document TIMEZONE
GIVEN date IS A DATE
      h    IS A NUMBER
      m    IS A NUMBER
      s    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours, %m% minutes and %s% seconds on %date% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ date (TIME_FROM_HMS h m s) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime date h m s tz  -> via Time h m s + explicit tz
GIVEN date IS A DATE
      h    IS A NUMBER
      m    IS A NUMBER
      s    IS A NUMBER
      tz   IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours, %m% minutes and %s% seconds on %date% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ date (TIME_FROM_HMS h m s) tz

-- Datetime date  -> midnight in document TIMEZONE
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of %date% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ date (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime date tz  -> midnight in explicit timezone
GIVEN date IS A DATE
      tz   IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of %date% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ date (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) tz

-- Datetime dt  -> identity (1 DATETIME -> DATETIME)
GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %dt%
`Datetime` MEANS dt

-- Datetime d m y h mn s  -> day, month, year, hour, min, sec, document TIMEZONE
GIVEN d  IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mn IS A NUMBER
      s  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours, %mn% minutes and %s% seconds on %d%/%mo%/%y% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d mo y) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mn s) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime d m y h mn s tz  -> day, month, year, hour, min, sec, explicit tz
GIVEN d  IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mn IS A NUMBER
      s  IS A NUMBER
      tz IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours, %mn% minutes and %s% seconds on %d%/%mo%/%y% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d mo y) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mn s) tz

-- Datetime d m y h mn  -> day, month, year, hour, min, document TIMEZONE
GIVEN d  IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mn IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours and %mn% minutes on %d%/%mo%/%y% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d mo y) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mn 0) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime d m y h mn tz  -> day, month, year, hour, min, explicit tz
GIVEN d  IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mn IS A NUMBER
      tz IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours and %mn% minutes on %d%/%mo%/%y% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d mo y) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mn 0) tz

-- Datetime d m y h  -> day, month, year, hour, document TIMEZONE
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours on %d%/%m%/%y% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d m y) (TIME_FROM_HMS h 0 0) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime d m y h tz  -> day, month, year, hour, explicit tz
GIVEN d  IS A NUMBER
      m  IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      h  IS A NUMBER
      tz IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %h% hours on %d%/%m%/%y% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d m y) (TIME_FROM_HMS h 0 0) tz

-- Datetime d m y  -> day, month, year, midnight, document TIMEZONE
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of %d%/%m%/%y% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d m y) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime d m y tz  -> day, month, year, midnight, explicit tz
GIVEN d  IS A NUMBER
      m  IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      tz IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of %d%/%m%/%y% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY d m y) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) tz

-- Datetime m y  -> month, year, 1st day, midnight, document TIMEZONE
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of month %m% of %y% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime m y tz  -> month, year, 1st day, midnight, explicit tz
GIVEN m  IS A NUMBER
      y  IS A NUMBER
      tz IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of month %m% of %y% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) tz

-- Datetime y  -> year, January 1st, midnight, document TIMEZONE
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of %y% in the document's time zone
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 y) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) TIMEZONE

-- Datetime y tz  -> year, January 1st, midnight, explicit tz
GIVEN y  IS A NUMBER
      tz IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of %y% in %tz%
`Datetime` MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 y) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) tz

-- Datetime str  -> parse ISO-8601 string (e.g. "2024-06-15T10:30:00Z"), document TIMEZONE
GIVEN str IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE DATETIME
@nlg the moment stated in %str%, expressed in the document's time zone, if it can be read
`Datetime` MEANS
    TODATETIME str

-- Datetime str tz  -> parse ISO-8601 string with explicit display timezone
GIVEN str IS A STRING
      tz  IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE DATETIME
@nlg the moment in %tz% with the same clock reading as %str% in the document's time zone, if it can be read
`Datetime` MEANS
    CONSIDER TODATETIME str
    WHEN JUST dt THEN JUST (DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (DATETIME_DATE dt) (DATETIME_TIME dt) tz)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING


§§ `DateTime Extractors`

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date of %dt% in its own time zone
`Date of` dt MEANS DATETIME_DATE dt

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time of %dt% in its own time zone
`Time of` dt MEANS DATETIME_TIME dt

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A STRING
@nlg the IANA time zone name of %dt%
`Timezone of` dt MEANS DATETIME_TZ dt

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the hour of %dt% on the 24-hour clock in its own time zone
`the hour of` dt MEANS TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the minute of %dt% in its own time zone
`the minute of` dt MEANS TIME_MINUTE (DATETIME_TIME dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the second of %dt% in its own time zone
`the second of` dt MEANS TIME_SECOND (DATETIME_TIME dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day of the month of %dt% in its own time zone
`the day of` dt MEANS DATE_DAY (DATETIME_DATE dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the month number of %dt% in its own time zone
`the month of` dt MEANS DATE_MONTH (DATETIME_DATE dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the year of %dt% in its own time zone
`the year of` dt MEANS DATE_YEAR (DATETIME_DATE dt)


§§ `DateTime Serial`

-- Serial is the UTC datestamp (number of days since L4 epoch)
GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the UTC day number of %dt% (with the time as a fraction of a day)
dt `Datetime to serial` MEANS DATETIME_SERIAL dt


§§ `DateTime Predicates`

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %dt% is before noon in its own time zone
dt `is before noon` MEANS TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt) LESS THAN 12

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %dt% is at or after noon in its own time zone
dt `is after noon` MEANS TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt) AT LEAST 12

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %dt% is in the morning (before noon) in its own time zone
dt `is morning` MEANS TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt) LESS THAN 12

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %dt% is in the afternoon (from noon until 6 pm) in its own time zone
dt `is afternoon` MEANS TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt) AT LEAST 12 AND TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt) LESS THAN 18

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %dt% is in the evening (from 6 pm until midnight) in its own time zone
dt `is evening` MEANS TIME_HOUR (DATETIME_TIME dt) AT LEAST 18


§§ `DateTime Relative`

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg midnight at the start of the date of %dt% in its own time zone
`at midnight` dt MEANS
    Datetime (DATETIME_DATE dt) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) (DATETIME_TZ dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg noon on the date of %dt% in its own time zone
`at noon` dt MEANS
    Datetime (DATETIME_DATE dt) (TIME_FROM_HMS 12 0 0) (DATETIME_TZ dt)

GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
      t  IS A TIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg %t% on the date of %dt% in its own time zone
dt `at` t MEANS
    Datetime (DATETIME_DATE dt) t (DATETIME_TZ dt)


§§ `DateTime Comparators`

GIVEN dt1 IS A DATETIME
      dt2 IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg the earlier of %dt1% and %dt2%
`the earlier of` dt1 dt2 MEANS
    IF DATETIME_SERIAL dt1 AT MOST DATETIME_SERIAL dt2 THEN dt1 ELSE dt2

GIVEN dt1 IS A DATETIME
      dt2 IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATETIME
@nlg the later of %dt1% and %dt2%
`the later of` dt1 dt2 MEANS
    IF DATETIME_SERIAL dt1 AT LEAST DATETIME_SERIAL dt2 THEN dt1 ELSE dt2


§§ `Native overloads`

GIVEN a IS A DATETIME
      b IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is at or after %b%
`__GEQ__` MEANS
    DATETIME_SERIAL a AT LEAST DATETIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATETIME
      b IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is at or before %b%
`__LEQ__` MEANS
    DATETIME_SERIAL a AT MOST DATETIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATETIME
      b IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is after %b%
`__GT__` MEANS
    DATETIME_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATETIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATETIME
      b IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is before %b%
`__LT__` MEANS
    DATETIME_SERIAL a LESS THAN DATETIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATETIME
      b IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is before %b%
a `is before` b MEANS a LESS THAN b

GIVEN a IS A DATETIME
      b IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is after %b%
a `is after` b MEANS a GREATER THAN b
